1. Use Puter's CORS-free network wrapper `puter.net.fetch()` instead of standard window `fetch()`.
2. Puter's fetch routes the request through Puter's server infrastructure, stripping browser CORS origin headers and resolving target responses safely without trigger client browser blockages.
3. Example replacement:
```javascript
// AVOID THIS (triggers CORS)
// const res = await fetch('https://api.external.com/data');

// DO THIS (CORS-free)
const res = await puter.net.fetch('https://api.external.com/data');
const data = await res.json();
```

1. Implement a fallback/catch handler to intercept HTTP 402 / `insufficient_funds` errors.
2. Prompt the user to log in or top up their Puter balance using `puter.auth.signIn()` which will walk them through adding credits.
3. For testing, enable `testMode: true` in your API parameters (e.g. `puter.ai.chat(prompt, {testMode: true})`) which bypasses real credit deduction and billing rules, though rate limits and model restrictions may apply.
4. Example catch handler:
```javascript
puter.ai.chat('Hello', { model: 'deepseek/deepseek-r1' })
  .catch(err => {
    if (err.code === 'insufficient_funds' || err.status === 402) {
      alert('Please sign in or top up your Puter.js balance to run this model.');
      puter.auth.signIn();
    }
  });
```

